;; /drive (RFC-073 "The drive loop", byj-71w.6): work through this project's
;; goal under its profile, through agent$drive. A turn, as every command that
;; stands for an agent is (RFC-004): the session's agent asks agent$drive to
;; run, reads its report, and says it.
;;
;; `/drive` alone works until the profile says to stop; `/drive WORDS` passes
;; the words along, though the run itself is the profile's and the beads'.
{:command "/drive"
 :agent "drive"
 :rephrase :predictor

 :default-request
 "Work through this project's goal as its profile allows."

 :purpose
 "work through this project's goal one bead at a time, as its profile (.brainyard/profile.edn, shown in AGENTS.md) allows — each ready bead worked, checked and closed, asking the person only where the profile says to"

 :usage
 "Call agent$drive with :question set to the request and read its report: each bead it worked on and how that ended, why it stopped, and what is still open. Do not work on beads yourself around it. When it stopped on a question for the person, end with that question as it put it. End with its report as it said it."

 :template
 "{request}

[{command}] This is {command}: {purpose}. {usage}"}
